							<p align="center"><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3" size="5"><strong><img src="/pics/2103/becomesoldier.jpg" /><br />Joining the Ranks</strong></font></p> <p><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3"></font>&nbsp;</p> <p><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3">For those few players that do beleive they can become a Soldier member there is a short process that must be done in accordance with our beleifs to become one of us in this family.</font></p> <p><font face="Verdana" color="#ffff00"><strong>{{{Note: Application is closed for ALL melee classes.&nbsp;If you are a Priest, Mage, Warlock, or Druid you are welcome to apply. Melee characters can still apply and exceptions may be made by an&nbsp;Officer or Guild Leader.}}}&nbsp;</strong></font></p> <p align="left"><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; First, a prospective Soldier must contact an Officer in game, these are&nbsp;<font color="#ffa500">Wars</font> (Guild Leader), <font color="#ff1493">Nikou</font>, <font color="#0000ff">Gospel</font>, <font color="#ff0000">Gartoggy</font> and <font color="#008000">Ziga</font>. This officer will decide whether or not the player seems like a Soldier through a brief interview.&nbsp;After this the prospective member will be required to post an introduction on the website in this <font color="#d3d3d3">thread:</font></font></p> <p align="left"><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3"><a href="/forums/threadlist.aspx?fid=3267">http://soldier.guildwizard.com/forums/threadlist.aspx?fid=3267</a></font></p> <p align="left"><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3"><font color="#d3d3d3">Upon completion of this introduction an&nbsp;Officer will propose a vote of</font> accepting or rejecting the prospective member to the guild in which <strong>2/3</strong> or more than <strong>2/3</strong> must be in accordance of accepting the new recruit.&nbsp; </font></p> <p align="left"><font face="Verdana" color="#ffff00"><strong>{{{Note: The application is not up yet, so filling out the application is not part of the application process right now.}}}</strong></font></p> <p align="left"><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Once this process is completed and the guild has agreed to accept a player, they have a probationary period of one week in which they will be considered an applicant member. After the probationary week has passed and a member has proven themselves to be a Soldier they will be considered a full member. </font></p> <p align="left"><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; If a prospective member's initial vote fails to award them the <strong>required 2/3 approval</strong> they will be disallowed to apply for membership until a month has passed. </font></p> <p align="left"><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Other things that a new recruit should consider before becoming a member are:</font></p> <p align="left"><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3"><font color="#ff0000">A Soldier's Oath</font> page located at: <a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1573"><font color="#d3d3d3">http://soldier.guildwizard.com/custom.aspx?pid=1573</font></a></font></p> <p align="left"><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3">The <font color="#008000">Raid Explanation</font> page located at: <a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1584"><font color="#d3d3d3">http://soldier.guildwizard.com/custom.aspx?pid=1584</font></a></font></p> <p align="left"><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3">The <font color="#0000ff">Guild FAQ</font> located at: </font><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3">&nbsp;<a href="/custom.aspx?pid=1575"><font color="#d3d3d3">http://soldier.guildwizard.com/custom.aspx?pid=1575</font></a></font></p> <p align="left"><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; If at any time a prospective Soldier does anything to shame the reputation of the guild or does anythign the guild would not deem in their best interest this is <strong><em>AUTOMATIC</em></strong> grounds for removal and will in no circumstance be tolerated. Examples of this would be Kill Stealing, Hacking, Engaging in public Flaming, etc. </font></p> <p align="left"><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3" size="4"><font size="3">Thank you and we hope to hear from you soon,</font> </font></p> <p align="left"><font face="Verdana" color="#d3d3d3" size="4">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font color="#0000ff"> -The Soldier Staff</font></font></p>
							
